83 to 2009 the subject has been taught both in HS and Degree level. From 2009 the Assamese subject has been taught only under graduate students. Prof.  Dilip Kumar Sarma was a first teacher of the department. Assamese is an also Elective Language subject at Degree level. Which was permitted by the G.U. Prof. Dilip Kumar Sarma was first Head of the Department.\nVision:- Overall development in the field of Assamese Language, Literature and Culture for impressive quantitative growth in Higher Education.\nMoto:- Quality practice and quality thinking.\nDate of Permission:- 1997-98\nDate of Govt Concurrence:-15-05-2000\nActivities:- The Department has organized seminar, workshop and many awareness programme for the development of students and society.\nInfrastructure:- It is located on well furnished RCC building ground floor (2nd block)\nFaculty Members\nDR BHASKAR PATGIRI\nDesignation\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR\nPhone\n9864139744\nEmail\nbpmilassam@gmail.com\nView Profile\nDR. MRIGENDRA NATH SARMA\nDesignation\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR, HOD\nPhone\n9435144024\nEmail\nsarmamrigen006@gmail.com\nView Profile\nBHARATI DEVI\nDesignation\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR\nPhone\n9864491624\nEmail\nbharatidevi2@gmail.com\nView Profile\nSyllabus\nTitle\nAction\nRegular Course\nView\nHonours Course\nView\nAchievements\nTitle\nDate\nAction\nCourse & Program Outcomes\nTitle\nAction\nActivities\nTitle\nDescription\nAction\nPrevious Year Question\nTitle\nDescription\nAction\nEx-faculty\nName\nPhoto\nBeltola College — Footer Demo\nBeltola College\nA premier institution of higher learning committed to excellence,\r\n          research, and holistic development of students since 1983.\n𝕗\n𝕏\n📷\n▶\nin\nQuick Links\n→ About the Institution\n→ Academic Programs\n→ Admissions 2026–27\n→ Research & Publications\n→ Placements\n→ Alumni Network\nImportant Links\n→ Student Portal\n→ Examination Committee\n→ IQAC\n→ Anti-Ragging Cell\n→ AQAR Reports\n→ RTI\nContact Us\n📍\nBeltola, Guwahati – 781028, Assam, India\n📞\n9